From 84c92edc74c25a17d8eddc030e0d4dded1d48910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohan <kharade@eurecom.fr>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:32:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pcf): rule reports of the SMF notify the AF

When the SMF reports PCC rules as no longer active (Npcf_SMPolicyControl_Update
with ruleReports, ruleStatus INACTIVE, e.g. failureCode RES_ALLO_FAIL when the
NG-RAN refused the QoS flow; TS 29.512 4.2.4.1, 5.6.2.7):

- the rules and their QoS decisions are removed from the association's
  decision, without a notification back to the SMF, which already removed them;
- for each app session the rules belong to (mcx-<app session ID>-<media
  component number>), the AF gets Npcf_PolicyAuthorization_Notify, POST
  {notifUri}/notify with an EventsNotification (TS 29.514 4.2.5.4, 5.6.2.5):
  event FAILED_RESOURCES_ALLOCATION and the media components as
  failedResourcAllocReports (mcResourcStatus INACTIVE), if the AF subscribed to
  that event in evSubsc.

The policy authorization service gets the report through a new pcf_event
signal (pa_rule_report), emitted after the association lock is released.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013UXVKWJNq3UC36dmrQjjV3
